text:
maya: Heads-up — the NextKit edge starter (Edge runtime + LangChain bridge) is flaking the eval harness intermittently. Repro steps below.

omar: I saw a failing run earlier. Is it the auth refresh flow or streaming socket termination?

maya: Seems auth + retry. In dev the client request sometimes gets a 401 during token rotation, our SDK retries but with the old token. Eval harness records truncated outputs.

paul_dev: Paste the server/api fetch snippet from the starter so I can check header wiring.

maya: Sure:```js
export default async function handler(req, res) {
  const prompt = await req.json().prompt;
  const r = await fetch(process.env.REDWOOD_API_URL + '/v1/generate', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY}`
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({ prompt })
  });
  const body = await r.text();
  res.status(r.status).send(body);
}
```

rachel: Note: the starter marks the API route with `export const runtime = 'edge'`. On some platforms process.env isn't available in the same way in edge builds. That might explain missing auth header.

samir: Also the starter pins SDK to v0.12.1. v0.12.3 had an auth-refresh bugfix. If edge+old-sdk race during refresh, token swap could fail.

omar: So two vectors: runtime env surface + SDK parity. Which is lowest friction for new users — switch runtime to node or bump SDK?

paul_dev: Bump the SDK to 0.12.3 in the starter (easy), and add an explicit runtime note in README. Also add a clear guard in the route:```js
if (!process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY) {
  throw new Error('REDWOOD_API_KEY missing — set in .env.local or use a server runtime for this route');
}
```

rachel: And tweak the eval harness: currently it treats any non-200 as immediate failure. Change harness to retry 401 with exponential backoff and trigger a token refresh path, so transient refresh races won't flake the job.

samir: I'll open a tiny PR: bump SDK, add README section "Edge runtime gotchas", and add the env-guard + small logging that surfaces missing auth header.

maya: I'll link the failing CI run: https://ci.internal/runs/8342 (shows truncated generated text). Marking job flaky until we have a fix.

devex-bot: Created issue #1482: "nextkit-edge-starter: auth refresh race + edge runtime causes intermittent 401 in eval harness" assigned to samir — https://issues.redwood/1482

omar: One more request — let's add an integration test that boots the sample in edge mode locally and simulates token expiry (msw mock), asserting the SDK refresh path is exercised. Minimal but would have caught this.

paul_dev: Agree. I'll sketch a test using msw to mock the token endpoint and force a 401 on first request, then succeed on refresh. Test asserts request flow and that no truncated output is returned.

rachel: Once PR lands I'll re-run the harness and de-flake the CI job. Thanks for the catch. :rocket:
